# RONDB-1124: a TC node failure in a wait of
# NdbQueryImpl::closeTcCursor() that makes every worker final
# (testJoinAggNdbApi Test 28).  The DBUG keyword
# ndb_query_close_nodefail_at_end makes such a wait report a node
# failure, as when the TC node disconnects in the poll that delivers
# the final EndOfData: in the wait for DBTC's answer to the close of a
# pushed join read until its first batches were used up, and in the
# wait for the pure EndOfData of a join aggregation closed right after
# execute().  Each close must return with error 4028 on the
# transaction, and the next query must give the right result.  Before
# the fix a debug NDB API aborted on
# assert(m_finalWorkers < getWorkerCount()) in
# NdbQueryImpl::setFetchTerminated().  Debug only: the DBUG keyword
# needs a debug NDB API.
#
# The program's output goes to a file and only its result lines are
# compared.  A crash fails the --exec; a failed check prints a FAILED
# line and "Some tests FAILED", which differ from the result file.
--source include/have_ndb.inc
--source include/have_debug.inc

--let $close_nodefail_out = $MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/tmp/testJoinAggNdbApiCloseNodeFail.out
--echo Running testJoinAggNdbApi --only 28
--error 0,1
--exec $NDB_PUSH_AGG_DIR/testJoinAggNdbApi -c "$NDB_CONNECTSTRING" -m $MASTER_MYPORT --only 28 > $close_nodefail_out 2>&1
--exec grep -E "^(Test 28|FAILED|All tests|Some tests)" $close_nodefail_out
--remove_file $close_nodefail_out

# Clean up database created by test program
DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS test_db;
